# Vandeta MITM payload - redirect test: answer every plaintext request with a
# 302 so the client follows it on its own.
#
#   WiFi > Wifi Atks > MITM Attack > Payload > redirect-test.mitm > Target > phone > Start
#
# Sweep, forward and catch every plaintext request, point DNS at the board, then
# answer with a 302 instead of a page - the client follows it without a click.
# Safe to run against a lab network or a phone you own.
#
# Target is not set here on purpose: pick the phone on the page (or
# `mitm target 192.168.1.167`). "All devices" sweeps one host at a time.
#
# page -> redirect
#   `page *` answered with 200 + HTML; `redirect *` answers 302 + Location.
#   The Location is an https:// URL, so the client fetches it over its own
#   route and the engine never sees the follow-up request.
#
# forward auto keeps the target's internet: without it the poison cuts the
# device off and the 302 points at a URL it cannot reach.
#
# Any other URL works on the same line.
sweep 1500
forward auto
redirect * https://example.com/
dns * this
